{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530544-here-be-dragons","id":1530544,"title":"\"Here be Dragons\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-11T03:54:27-08:00","id":1530544,"title":"\"Here be Dragons\"","content":"Hic sunt dracones<br /> <br /> I must admit, I am not <i>that </i>familiar with the history and lore of the Fifth Edition, tho' I tries to keep an eye on it, but as it may happens several things tend to avoid my notice<br /> So in advance, please forgive my ignorace<br /> <br /> As you probably guessed, my question are about the Tzimisce<br /> Why the Tzimisce left the Sabbat (if they left at all) and joined the Anarchs?<br /> So tried to form a few theory<br /> I am quite familiar with the Clan and aware the current incarnation was born in the fires of the <b>Anarch Revolt </b>and the Sabbat formed from the remnants of the Anarch Revolt of the time.<br /> The Tzimisce would not cede their lands to the hated Tremere and submit the philosophy of Metamorphosism for the limited ideals of Humanity, while the Lasombra had invested too much in the Revolt to surrender their success to decrepit elders of other Clans<br /> It was a logical step<br /> With their Antediluvians dead to form a sect devoted to warfare against the Antediluvians and the tyranny of their catspaws<br /> Nice story, tho' the higher up one goes in the Sabbat ranks the &quot;us against the world&quot; outlook of the young packs became more and more &quot;me against the world&quot;. In order to survive long enough to achieve position and age within the sect, a vampire must learn how to live for themselves, and to fight for every scrap of profit or slightest advantage. Unlike the Camarilla, there was no rigid hierarchy in place to promote or control the ambitions of Sabbat vampires \u2013 the only rank and title a Sabbat holds is what they have the power to take.<br /> Both the Tzimisce and the Lasombra encourage this dog-eat-dog culture, as it seems to ensure that only the strongest, smartest, and most capable lead the sect, and all the rest are fodder for the appetites of their betters.<br /> The Elder Tzimisce of the Old World never really supported the whole Sabbat idea, paid off the youngs, or paid lip seervice but just wanted to be left alone<br /> Now the young Anarch Tzimisce who formed the Sabbat eventually became Elders themselves - the irony here is they learned the lessons what made their Sires the lord of the domains and became just like them - and their childrens grew tired of their hypocritical sires and elders who take up all the good resources and domains of the night. They were equally tired of their sires treating them as mere property.<br /> Be pre-V5 or V5, the Tzimisce always first and foremost were about ownership<br /> The Ventrue is about &quot;commanding&quot;, leading others.They treat as their destiny and entitlement and justify it by claiming to be the best fit to lead. It's their <i>responsibility</i> and what's best for everyone. They want to inspire loyalty. Their lineage is important because it's a way to inspire loyalty within the clan, to the clan. That makes the clan seem strong and respectable, which in turn makes the Ventrue that make up the clan all the more inspiring. They want others not only to serve their interests, but to even feel good about serving. They want people to seek them out for advice or leadership. That respect (or fear) is what is most important to them.<br /> The Lasombra are about &quot;using&quot; others. Where the Ventrue rule through leadership and authority, the Lasombra rule through power and coercion. The Lasombra could care less about &quot;loyalty.&quot; In fact, in a way they probably outright despise it. Showing loyalty just means you're holding back your own ambitions, which is far more useful to the clan. A Lasombra can, and will, use anything at its disposal in order to get you to do what it wants. The Lasombra will waste no time making you revile it, if that goads you into reckless behavior that leaves you vulnerable. The Lasombra will happily appear weak or even defeated for a chance at crushing whatever stands in its way.<br /> And the Tzimisce?<br /> The Tzimisce <i>own</i>. They don't consider themselves to obligated to their subjects and they aren't necessarily a means to an end. Ownership is the end. They could be efficient retainers. They could be pets or ornaments. What matters is that they're whatever the Tzimisce wants them to be, not if they need them or vice versa. And if anyone takes them or any other property away, they're not a victor who deserves the spoils, they're a reprehensible thief to be painfully destroyed or enslaved.<br /> The Tzimisce are about ownership. They don't care about results. They don't care about inspiration. They care about total control. They want you to live every waking moment knowing you exist at their whims. Their clan's obsession with manners is a mirror of exactly that. Enter a Tzimisce's home with gifts, and you will remain unharmed for three nights... because you are its guest. For those three nights, it is responsible for you. Therefore, it owns you. It doesn't matter the Tzimisce's subjects are loyal because of love, because of fear, because of ancient oaths, because of Koldunic magic, because of blood bonds, because you fleshcrafted their brain into perfect servitude, because of stockholm syndrome...it makes no difference to the Tzimisce.<br /> What metters is to <i>own</i><br /> To possess and to dominate are two very different things.<br /> Dominating someone means bending that someone to your will, forcing or in any other means imposing your will unto them directly. It is closer to a relationship of master and slave. One controls, the other obeys.<br /> Possessing is a little different in subtlety. When you possess someone, it does not mean you dominate them. It means you own them. While dominating someone implies you use them, simply possessing them implies, one way or another, they are part of your property, it necessarily the tool you use.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are hoarders and bound to the land they own.<br /> This has been established for a long time.<br /> Their proficiency in blood bonds which they cultivated to an artform and their clan bane actively enforce this idea.<br /> The companion merely introduced the concept of obsession. It is made very clear the Tzimisce covet things for the sake of owning them, as in adding them to their collection, as opposed to using them because it furthers goals (as the Lasombra). It is, as stated, like a Dragon who needs its treasure.<br /> This leads to them having estates that look dilapidated for they care not what happens there, only that they <i>have them</i>, and so on.<br /> <br /> As for leadership, this was always the case (they are sabbat founders and former nobility). They are old fashioned and set in their ways, with their hospitality rules and the burden of rulership.<br /> A ruler <i>is not </i>a master.<br /> A ruler cares for the domain but usually does not actively involve oneself in its day to day life.<br /> If threatened, a Tzimisce will protect what is theirs and impose their rules, but will not actively slave the population.<br /> To hear the hoariest tales, some Voivode lords suffused themselves into their homelands, merging their consciousness with the very soil of the domain.<br /> <i>What better way to show ownership of the land and its folk than to become that very land and sustain the generations to come?</i><br /> One thing to remember is that the clan has actually always partially tended towards that direction.<br /> They have always been the overlords ruling over peasant villages from ancient castles. We as players have known them as metamorphosists, but pretty much every book noted that there were actually rather few followers of that path, with most Tzimisce using the discipline without applying greater philosophy to it and subscribing to transhumanism only in a very general &quot;We're better than the Herd&quot; sort of way.<br /> <br /> SO the new young Anarch Tzimsice strive to redefine themselves by what they rule over. They set out to found their own holdings and be their own masters in the night.<br /> <br /> But... and here comes my question, why?<br /> Why the Anarch movement? <br /> <br /> You can't own other anarchs and in theory the whole notion of the Anarch Barons is an oxymoron!<br /> By its simplest definition, a Baron is the Anarch Movement\u2019s equivalent of a Prince. A Baron is a Kindred with all the responsibilities of a prince, but without the tools. He can\u2019t count on the respect that the prince\u2019s title inspires, because he doesn\u2019t have the strength of a prince. In addition to having less political clout than most princes, a baron isn\u2019t necessarily one of the eldest or most powerful Kindred in a region<br /> The Anarchs know that any territory with even a modest Kindred population requires someone to moderate it. Most of the Baron's time is devoted to mediating conflicts and disputes between Kindred, orchestrating agreements with other local Kindred leaders (both within the movement and the other sects) and enforcing those traditions that even the Anarchs must obey.<br /> Many Anarch barons hold the position because they feel a responsibility to the goals and well-being of the sect. Not for personal glory, nor for power over their fellow Kindred, but out of an actual sense of civic duty that most Kindred lost <br /> Now this... is not ownership.<br /> This is quite the opposite, your subjects <i>owns you</i><br /> <br /> From the logical point of view, the Tzimisce should be Camarilla!<br /> The Tremere are in ruins (the Salubri are back - and any self respecting Dragon should own a precious Unicorn) and the Nosferatu while like the Gangrel were seen interlopers on their lands, more often than not, a Nosferatu if introduced itself and accepted the Tzimisce lordship was treated like... just anyone else. Same with the Gangrel. In the Dark Ages this was something no other High Clan did and I belive this carried over in to the modern nights, not to mention both Clans were the victims of the Tremere Gargoyle experiments. While the Gangrel left, the Tzimisce basically age old allies are there - not to mention the Lasombra who jumped ship...<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce - overfond of traditions - logically should find the neofeudalism of the Camarilla attractive while the Anarch standpoint repulsive\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T12:18:41-08:00","id":1530573,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce Anarchs are probably close to a &quot;spirit of the frontier&quot; sort of mindset, anarchocapitalists of sort.<br /> <br /> They aggressively want their own space, their own domain, and aren't willing to submit to anyone. They want to be free to establish themselves as rulers of their small place, and will not bow to Camarilla hierarcs. They may have neighbours, with whom they trade and are willing to fight along against common foes. <br /> <br /> Their elders may be willing to re-join the Camarilla and take their place in a feudal hierarchy as the Old Clan. the youngsters, I see them as the unliving embodiment of &quot;Don't tread on me&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T12:47:25-08:00","id":1530577,"title":"","content":"Thanks for making this thread!<br /> <br /> The funny fact is that I don't THINK the Tzimisce HAVE joined the Anarchs and are just independent, aren't they?<br /> <br /> Yet every table, including my own, have been having them show up at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:24:06-08:00","id":1530586,"title":"","content":"According to players guide. The Tzismce are regarded as an independent clan in general. That said I see most of them only having transactional agreements with the Camarilla and Anarchs with the eldest and youngest maybe joining either sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T00:00:55-08:00","id":1530614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530544-here-be-dragons?p=1530577#post1530577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for making this thread!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530544-here-be-dragons?p=1530577#post1530577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny fact is that I don't THINK the Tzimisce HAVE joined the Anarchs and are just independent, aren't they?<br /> <br /> Yet every table, including my own, have been having them show up at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530544-here-be-dragons?p=1530586#post1530586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzismce are regarded as an independent clan in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5's corebook states that plenty of the Sabbat members defected to Anarchs during the beckoning for various reasons, but the Anarch book technically doesn't specifically discuss the Tzimisce's inclusion in the Anarch movement. There is a scene where some Anarch intrude into a Tzimisce lair they thought was abandoned and are captured. But there is no real discussion of how the Tzimisce would function as members of an Anarch city or group.<br /> And the Companion stated, many young Tzimisce have gone Anarch, finding their elders\u2019 and sires\u2019 greed hampers their own growt<br /> <br /> They are certanly Independent, if such thing even exist in the V5 setting...<br /> I mean In V5, everyone's forming up; formerly independent clans are joining established sects, and the necromancers just kind of went and made their own<br /> The Hecata is basically an independent necromantic sect, not a &quot;Clan&quot;<br /> I'm still not sure Mayumi Shibasaki is/was the de-facto Prince of Tokyo or just an Autarkis who exerted a great deal of influence over the city...<br /> <br /> Here lies my problem<br /> There are no &quot;real&quot; Independents in V5 as far as I see - the Ashirra allied with the Camarila, the Laibon Legacies of Africa not mentioned as far as I know, tho' the Anarch book and Cults of the Blood God mentions the Setite of Africa and the Orthodox Church of Set still calls themselves Followers of Set instead of Minsitry of Set <i>implying</i>\u200b there are African vampires and the Raktasadhu of India is something that was quietly forgotten, like the Drowned Legacies or the Einherjar of Skandinavia (tho' the later went a bit dormant after the fall of Uppsala to Christian converts and many Einherjar joined the Sabbat, but after Brunhilde awoke, a new group of neonates and anarchs calling themselves the Valkyrie has risen to prominence in Scandinavia, mimicking the ways of the Einherjar and trying to return to the old ways.) <br /> So my point is, or at least how I see it, in V5 you are either Anarch or either Camarilla (Sabbat, mayhaps if anything remained of it) but can't maintain your independence and call yourself really an Independent<br /> And the Camarilla don't really highlighted the Tzimisce so many players belive I think, they are probably Anarch - because there are no other choice really<br /> <br /> The strange is, a Camarilla Prince would benefit greatly if a Tzimisce would move in the neighborhood - a fiercely territorial neighbour, who rise literal hell if someone even dare to look at <i>her</i> Domain is someone you can count on. <br /> Let it take an estate and move in, Addams Family style - they're creepy and they're kooky, mysterious and spooky - and <i>recognize</i> and <i>respect </i>her domain's borders, maybe lobby for a re-forestation to have one around her estate where she could play (and if you are in to it, even the Lupines would be pleased with that, win win)\u200b and routinely collect (with her premission of course) the tresspassers' bodies who were made to be a fence<br /> It is like having a dragon living on your land, sure you have to be careful not to poke it, but no sane enemy would attack you risking its anger","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T01:24:42-08:00","id":1530617,"title":"","content":"I mean, that's not quite what it means because the Anarchs are anyone that is outside the Camarilla according to the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T02:35:34-08:00","id":1531281,"title":"","content":"Honestly, with the Second Inquisition raging, you\u2019d think the assorted factions would be tripping over themselves to get a flesh-crafter in their Domain. Hunters on your tail? Here\u2019s some new faces for you. All that intel on your appearance is now permanently useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T06:00:03-08:00","id":1531288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530544-here-be-dragons?p=1531281#post1531281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, with the Second Inquisition raging, you\u2019d think the assorted factions would be tripping over themselves to get a flesh-crafter in their Domain. Hunters on your tail? Here\u2019s some new faces for you. All that intel on your appearance is now permanently useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat having control over the Tzimisce for centuries didn't help them as the Clan has to deal with the fact they have a reputation as Ed Gein, Hannibal Lecter, and Rob Zombie versus more refined types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T12:16:36-08:00","id":1531302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530544-here-be-dragons?p=1531281#post1531281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, with the Second Inquisition raging, you\u2019d think the assorted factions would be tripping over themselves to get a flesh-crafter in their Domain. Hunters on your tail? Here\u2019s some new faces for you. All that intel on your appearance is now permanently useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shaper clan has a nick name called the Fiends for a reason and it's very well earned and most Kindred who still value there humanity somewhat will avoid dealing with them unless it's a last resort. Besides Obfuscate, makeup and little tricks such changing your body language or posture or changing your fashion sense can be as effective as flesh crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T01:39:57-08:00","id":1531945,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra were also known as the most vocal opponents of the Camarilla, but now they\u2019ve got a mass-exodus to the Camarilla, purging their elders and buddying up with the enemy in the name of survival. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T07:59:29-08:00","id":1531954,"title":"","content":"It is certainly good to see a detailed and good post in regard to Vampiresses and Vampires from Clan Tzimisce. I was definitely happy to see and hear about them being included in V5 as an important and noteworthy organization and group. The Tzimisce Kindred were and remain a key and essential group and faction in the VtM as an RPG and as a setting.<br /> <br /> Also I have to say that the title of this thread is a good and interesting use of an important and good phrase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T12:20:46-08:00","id":1531971,"title":"","content":"The Tzmisce (and the lasombra) are pretty hard to write for in 5th since both clans go against the hard pushed thematic tones of the Edition-they dont care about humanity on any level full stop and are politically/culturally very very Sabbat. This can be seen in how the writing is somewhat stunted in 5th ed were their write up is just old clan dracula tzmisce.<br /> <br /> But yeah the Camarilla is a 'better' fit than Anarchs, it's still bad fit but at least their's some overlap. IMO the best sect for them is revised Sabbat by a considerable margin but if I we to remove them from the sword they probably wouldn't even be in a sect but an independent clan re-establishing voivodes in eastern europe and former Sabbat domains were they'd incorporate the stragglers from the Sword as vassals using a mixture of dark age and Sabbat social order to consolidate power<br /> <br /> EDIT-the idea I did have for the Anarch tzmisce was they'd be the LGBTQ grouping in the clan, a lot of younger player are interested in viss for this sort of thing and I could easily see a dragon laying claim to urban gay villages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-04-2024, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[